---
import HubPage from '../components/HubPage.astro';
---
<HubPage hubId="corporate-finance">
  <section aria-labelledby="hub-guide" class="mt-12 max-w-3xl">
    <h2 id="hub-guide" class="text-xl font-bold text-text-primary mb-4">How to choose a corporate finance calculator</h2>
    <p class="text-sm text-text-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">Start with the discount rate. The <a href="/wacc-calculator" class="text-accent hover:underline font-medium">WACC calculator</a> gives the blended cost of capital that most firms use as the hurdle rate for new projects. Feed that rate into the <a href="/npv-calculator" class="text-accent hover:underline font-medium">NPV calculator</a>: a positive NPV means the project earns more than it costs to fund. The <a href="/irr-calculator" class="text-accent hover:underline font-medium">IRR calculator</a> returns the rate at which NPV is zero, which is easier to compare across projects but can mislead when cash flows change sign more than once.</p>
    <p class="text-sm text-text-muted leading-relaxed mb-4">For a quick risk check, <a href="/payback-period-calculator" class="text-accent hover:underline font-medium">payback period</a> shows how many years it takes to recover the outlay, and <a href="/discounted-payback-period-calculator" class="text-accent hover:underline font-medium">discounted payback</a> does the same after discounting, so it is never shorter. To value a whole business, the <a href="/dcf-calculator" class="text-accent hover:underline font-medium">DCF calculator</a> adds a terminal value to projected cash flows. <a href="/present-value-calculator" class="text-accent hover:underline font-medium">Present value</a> and <a href="/future-value-calculator" class="text-accent hover:underline font-medium">future value</a> handle single amounts, such as what a payment due in five years is worth today.</p>
  </section>
</HubPage>
